 "remarks": "The Gold Coast meets the Connecticut shoreline in this extraordinary Wilson Point estate, gracefully perched to capture water views stretching to Long Island Sound. Built in 1924, this English Tudor Manor-style residence is one of the original homes in the coveted Wilson Point Association, offering timeless architecture, rich character, and an exceptional sense of history. The home features four/five bedrooms, four full baths, sun-filled living spaces where nearly every window frames picturesque views of the surrounding landscape, an office, and bonus spaces. A charming fenced kitchen garden and an enclosed vegetable garden awaits the gardener and chef alike. Just steps from the private beach, clubhouse, and tennis courts, this spectacular property offers multiple terraces for entertaining, perennial gardens, and an expansive lawn, creating an idyllic setting for relaxing, gathering with family and friends, and enjoying the best of Connecticut coastal living. A prime location for an easy commute to NYC - just 47 minutes to Grand Central from Rowayton - the closest train station and a 3-minute drive. Wilson Point provides the ultimate privacy along with dock, and boat mooring options.",
